  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">amandla.mobi is an advocacy network of black South African women who use mobile phones and organizing tactics to advance relevant issues, holding decision makers accountable to their commitments. amandla.mobi&#x2019;s priorities over the next three years include cultivating the next generation of organizers while deepening solidarity across its more than 900,000 active members to support campaigns on issues of health care, education, sanitation, and gender-based violence. (Strategy: Transparency, Participation, and Accountability)</narrative>
  </description>
